278
00:20:17,625 --> 00:20:19,583
Mom is just your excuse.

279
00:20:19,666 --> 00:20:23,291
You just don’t want me and Mom
to be here. Am I right?

280
00:20:23,375 --> 00:20:25,458
-That’s not what I mean.
-Then what?

281
00:20:25,541 --> 00:20:29,125
I don't und…Tell me then!

282
00:20:29,208 --> 00:20:32,083
What’s actually going on in your head
I don't get it!

283
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:34,750
What?

284
00:20:40,125 --> 00:20:41,083
Follow me!

285
00:20:41,583 --> 00:20:42,500
Come on.

286
00:20:43,375 --> 00:20:44,875
You want to know? Come!

287
00:20:59,916 --> 00:21:01,916
Five years, Laras!

288
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,375
Five years I was chasing these!

289
00:21:06,291 --> 00:21:12,500
MISSING PERSON - SURABAYA

290
00:21:19,791 --> 00:21:21,416
MISSING PERSON - SURABAYA

291
00:21:23,291 --> 00:21:26,250
In 2004, right around the time Dad died,

292
00:21:26,333 --> 00:21:27,791
there were reports
of workers disappearing…

293
00:21:29,125 --> 00:21:30,583
In Surabaya…

294
00:21:34,625 --> 00:21:35,875
And Madura.

295
00:21:35,958 --> 00:21:38,208
MISSING PEOPLE IN MADURA

296
00:21:38,791 --> 00:21:39,666
Right?

297
00:21:40,958 --> 00:21:43,833
Fourteen people! It's fourteen!

298
00:21:43,916 --> 00:21:45,708
He must be one of them.

299
00:21:46,958 --> 00:21:48,875
And there’s still no clarity!

300
00:21:52,791 --> 00:21:57,083
Every year, people go missing--
and it keeps getting covered up.

301
00:21:57,166 --> 00:22:00,458
But it feels odd.
Every missing worker happens…

302
00:22:00,958 --> 00:22:03,083
It happened around the night of Suro.

303
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:09,000
And I don’t understand
what the connection is.

304
00:22:10,833 --> 00:22:14,333
This is strange, Laras.
It doesn't make sense!

305
00:23:16,875 --> 00:23:18,750
WELCOME TO THE BRIDGE PROJECT

306
00:23:18,833 --> 00:23:20,333
YOU ARE ENTERING MANDATORY PPE AREA

307
00:23:31,916 --> 00:23:33,125
